---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_626",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 626,
  "text": "[[2758.12]] <b>492₁.  Modalia et elementa juris naturalis. Erste Fassung </p>\n<p> [[2758.18]] <b>Justitia</b> est charitas recte ordinata seu virtus servans rationem in affectu erga alios\n[[2758.19]] ratione praeditos. </p>\n<p> [[2758.20]] <b>Vir bonus</b> est qui justitia praeditus est. Omnis prudens est vir bonus. </p>\n<p> [[2758.21]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character><b>Indebitum</b> <tab/>est, quod viro bono qua tali <tab/>^&.b</b> <Leibniz special character> </p>\n<p> [[2758.22]] <b>Debitum</b> <tab/><picture>204</picture> <tab/><picture>304</picture> <tab/>necessarium </p>\n<p> [[2758.23]] <b>Indebitum</b> <tab/>contingens </p>\n<p> [[2758.24]] <tab/>est, quod viro bono qua tali </p>\n<p> [[2758.25]] <b>Licitum</b> <tab/>possibile </p>\n<p> [[2758.26]] <b>Illicitum</b> <tab/>impossibile. </p>\n<p> [[2758.27]] Hinc omnes propositiones Logicae circa Modales huc transferri possunt: ex. grat.\n[[2759.1]] <petit> </p>\n<p> [[2759.2]] <i>Der in Kleindruck folgende Text wurde von Leibniz später ersetzt</i>: </p>\n<p> [[2759.3]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character><tab/>Quod viro prudenti <tab/>necessarium <tab/>etiam viro bono <tab/>necessarium <tab/>est^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character>\n [[2759.4]] <tab/><picture>504</picture> <tab/>necessarium <tab/><picture>404</picture> <tab/><picture>504</picture> <tab/>necessarium <tab/><picture>404</picture> </p>\n<p> [[2759.5]] <tab/>contingens <tab/>contingens </p>\n<p> [[2759.6]] <tab/>Quod viro prudenti <tab/>etiam viro bono <tab/>est licet non contra. </p>\n<p> [[2759.7]] <tab/>possibile <tab/>possibile </p>\n<p> [[2759.8]] <tab/>impossibile <tab/>impossibile\n [[2759.9]] <tab/>Hinc omnes propositiones [<i>bricht ab</i>] </p>\n<p> [[2759.10]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character><tab/>Quae viro bono <tab/>necessarium <tab/>etiam prudenti <tab/>necessarium^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character>\n [[2759.11]] <tab/><picture>503</picture> <tab/>necessarium <tab/><picture>403</picture> <tab/><picture>503</picture> <tab/>necessarium\n [[2759.12]] <tab/>Quae viro bono <tab/>possibile <tab/>etiam prudenti <tab/>possibile\n [[2759.13]] <tab/>impossibile <tab/>impossibile [<i>bricht ab</i>]\n[[2759.14]] <tab/>Vir bonus enim, etsi forte prudens non sit, agit tamen ut prudens in his quae ad bona malaque\n[[2759.15]] aliena pertinent. Sed prudentis officium latius patet. </p>\n<p> [[2759.16]] Nullum impossibile est debitum; seu impossibilium nulla est obligatio.\n [[2759.17]] <tab/>Nam omne impossibile est impossibile viro bono. Nullum impossibile viro bono utcunque est\n[[2759.18]] necessarium viro bono qua tali, jam necessarium viro bono qua tali idem est quod debitum. Ergo\n[[2759.19]] nullum impossibile est debitum. </p>\n<p> [[2759.20]] Omne necessarium est licitum; seu necessitas non habet legem.\n [[2759.21]] <tab/>Nam omne necessarium est necessarium viro bono. Omne necessarium viro bono utcunque est\n[[2759.22]] possibile viro bono qua tali; hoc est licitum. </petit> </p>\n<p> [[2759.23]] Omne debitum est licitum. </p>\n<p> [[2759.24]] Omne illicitum est indebitum. </p>\n<p> [[2759.25]] Nullum illicitum est debitum. </p>\n<p> [[2759.26]] Nullum debitum est illicitum.\n [[2759.27]] <tab/>Quia omne necessarium est possibile, omne impossibile est contingens seu\n[[2759.28]] potest non fieri. Nullum impossibile est necessarium. Nullum necessarium\n[[2759.29]] est impossibile. Ergo omne necessarium viro bono qua tali est possibile viro\n[[2759.30]] bono qua tali; et ita porro. </p>\n<p> [[2759.31]] Nullum impossibile est debitum, seu impossibilium nulla est obligatio.\n [[2759.32]] <tab/>Nam omne impossibile est impossibile viro bono. Nullum impossibile viro\n[[2759.33]] bono utcunque est possibile viro bono qua tali. Quod non est possibile viro\n[[2759.34]] bono qua tali non est necessarium viro bono qua tali, seu non est debitum. </p>\n<p> [[2759.35]] Omne necessarium est licitum, seu necessitas non habet legem.\n [[2759.36]] <tab/>Nam omne necessarium est necessarium viro bono. Quod est necessarium\n[[2760.1]] viro bono, ejus oppositum est impossibile viro bono. Quod impossibile viro\n[[2760.2]] bono utcunque non est possibile viro bono qua tali seu licitum. Ergo necessarii\n[[2760.3]] oppositum non est licitum. Cujus autem oppositum non est licitum, id\n[[2760.4]] ipsum est licitum. </p>\n",
  "number": "492₁.",
  "title": "Modalia et elementa juris naturalis. Erste Fassung",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:492₁. Modalia et elementa juris naturalis. Erste Fassung Justitia est charitas recte ordinata seu virtus servans rationem in affectu erga alios ratione praeditos. Vir bonus est qui justitia praeditus est. Omnis prudens est vir bonus. ^&.bb Indebitum est, quod viro bono qua tali ^&.b Debitum 204 304 ...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>